<title>GERMANY: Thyssen ends bourse down 10 pct at 375.5 marks.</title>
<headline>Thyssen ends bourse down 10 pct at 375.5 marks.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German engineering group Thyssen AG ended bourse trade on Tuesday down 10.06 percent at 375.50 marks after a hostile takeover bid by Krupp-Hoesch was shelved.</p>
<p>The overall DAX index ended bourse trade at 3,349.14 points, up 27.30 points or 0.82 percent.</p>
<p>Late on Monday, the two companies said after five days of talks they were planning to set up a joint steel venture and explore other areas of cooperation.</p>
<p>Krupp-Hoesch shares also ended the day lower, down 7.50 marks or 2.22 percent at 331 marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
